# The whole test, in three sections: the state, the act, the state it leaves.
#
# **`{given}`, `{when}` and `{then}` are markers.** Every row after one belongs to it, which is
# line order carrying grouping as well as sequence - Sean, 2026-09-15, on his own sketch of this
# file. **They carry no values**; the name is the whole of the row.
#
# **Nothing says to execute or to compare.** The sections say it: `when` is what the player does
# and `then` is what should be true afterwards.
#
# **The prologue is script rows and the sections are game rows**, which is why the script store is
# checked against the prologue alone.

